                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3c7b436-1b70-33d1-a57e-deeef2b25bd3",
                        "entry_id": "2080ec5f-52ad-3023-911d-a0ff3c40e8ad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Amateurish; characterized by overacting."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a682c75-76cf-446c-98f0-07a79d8af6fe",
                                "sense_id": "c3c7b436-1b70-33d1-a57e-deeef2b25bd3",
                                "text": "Jack Crawford: I’m Special Agent Jack Crawford. I lead the Behavioral Science Unit.\nWill Graham: We’ve met.\nJack Crawford: Yes, we had a disagreement about the museum when we opened it.\nWill Graham: I disagreed with what you named it.\nJack Crawford: The Evil Minds Research Museum?\nWill Graham: It’s a little hammy, Jack."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09785da4-cf6d-47b3-b5c4-74853cd05b68",
                                "sense_id": "c3c7b436-1b70-33d1-a57e-deeef2b25bd3",
                                "text": "McDonald & Dodds is back, with episode one so deliberately hammy and meta that, technically, it should have been a complete horlicks. In one scene, when they were all hanging on to the balloon ropes, Mr Bean-like, to stop Jason Watkins flying away, it sort of was."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
