            {
                "entry_id": "2366a442-8695-392f-a5e8-bab838054b80",
                "word": "hammy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "75b0a739-9af5-48e4-a2ca-3600aae75df3",
                        "entry_id": "2366a442-8695-392f-a5e8-bab838054b80",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hammies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "874b0107-fbf1-3f72-9a3d-585384e89cf5",
                        "entry_id": "2366a442-8695-392f-a5e8-bab838054b80",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The hamstring."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "US",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2b9a976-932f-4f5b-bca9-0b794ca7f87d",
                                "sense_id": "874b0107-fbf1-3f72-9a3d-585384e89cf5",
                                "text": "He put his palms flat on the ground, then grabbed the back of his knees, stretching his hammies for the millionth time that morning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc7bd590-f3e5-44f4-aac3-e02d7f8972d9",
                                "sense_id": "874b0107-fbf1-3f72-9a3d-585384e89cf5",
                                "text": "“A move like this would have been inpossible for me before yoga,” he said. “Flexibilty-wise, I was struggling. My hammies were tight, my groin was tight. My hips have really benefited.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "127ea68c-7a04-444a-816d-295b6f0eaa64",
                                "sense_id": "874b0107-fbf1-3f72-9a3d-585384e89cf5",
                                "text": "I've noticed that although cycling keeps me reasonably \"cardio fit\", I am losing general flexibility, e.g. when touching my toes. This is despite me stretching my quads, calves, and hammies during and after my training rides."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83f5f305-7f25-49e7-a1db-b58e3c5d502b",
                                "sense_id": "874b0107-fbf1-3f72-9a3d-585384e89cf5",
                                "text": "2004, J. L. Roberts, Braggin' Rights: Fantasy Football Rewind 2004 (2003 Season Recap), AuthorHouse USA, page 83,\nA slow start and hammy injury were major contributors."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d92038e4-399e-37da-beb0-1c4e65265840",
                        "entry_id": "2366a442-8695-392f-a5e8-bab838054b80",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A hamstring injury."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "US",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ff4dc39-b18d-4ae4-8df0-a93f8112c52f",
                                "sense_id": "d92038e4-399e-37da-beb0-1c4e65265840",
                                "text": "A: I′m only just getting fully fit now after that hammy [hamstring tear]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "142046f1-b9a6-4350-9196-9cd16570e678",
                                "sense_id": "d92038e4-399e-37da-beb0-1c4e65265840",
                                "text": "Why he went back on after 3/4 time is beyond me. If he was trying to prove a point he has all season to do that not do your hammy in the first game."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
